WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Start with the assessment scope. Bring domains, IP addresses, and exposed services into an inventory the security team can investigate.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Attach service information and relevant vulnerability data. A version match is a lead for investigation; exploitability still needs validation.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Consider exposure, supporting evidence, and the affected service together. Keep uncertainty visible so the team understands the priority.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
Carry the affected asset, evidence, and remediation context into the report. Give the responsible engineering team enough information to act.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
At Invia, I owned product architecture and security design, defined the discovery and analysis pipeline, and helped take CyberShield360 to launch.
